WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.450
Another stats dashboard. Go on — ask.

2
00:00:03.350 --> 00:00:06.350
Across F3, men show up before dawn to work out.

3
00:00:06.350 --> 00:00:08.350
Each leaves a row of data.

4
00:00:08.350 --> 00:00:10.900
PAX Vault turns those rows into a story.

5
00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:13.300
Region leaders see the whole picture.

6
00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:16.350
Real growth, who's leading, and where new men come from.

7
00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:19.000
The site Q sees his own AO.

8
00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:22.400
The strong days, and the site that's fading before it goes dark.

9
00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:24.700
Every man gets his own record.

10
00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:27.750
His posts, the men he's met, the day he first showed up.

11
00:00:28.110 --> 00:00:29.500
Here's why it matters.

12
00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:31.900
When a man goes quiet, the data notices.

13
00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:34.550
So his leaders can go back, and pick up the six.

14
00:00:34.950 --> 00:00:38.400
And when someone's three posts from five hundred, nobody misses it.

15
00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:39.600
They celebrate it.

16
00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:42.550
PAX Vault. The story inside the data.
